# {{lb|en|intransitive|aviation}} To [[roll]] or [[incline]] laterally in order to [[turn]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/02/world/middleeast/flydubai-attack-timeline.html?smid=nytcore-android-share|work=The New York Times|passage=Mr. Hayoun, the plumber, 50, heard Ms. Manes scream “He’s stabbing him!” His first thought, he said, was that one passenger was attacking another. “And at the very moment I stand up and step out of my seat, the plane '''banks''' — '''banks''' very sharply to the left — and then levels out again,” he told Kan 11, Israel’s public broadcaster. “That shook me.”|title=The Mother’s Scream That Sent Passengers to the Rescue|date=2026-10-02|author=David M. Halbfinger|accessdate=2026-10-05|author2=Natan Odenheimer|author3=Adam Rasgon|author4=Johnatan Reiss|author5=Aaron Boxerman}}
